      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Phoenix Suns, the city’s first major sports franchise, began playing in 1968 and moved from the Coliseum to America West Arena in 1992.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 2008, the city’s second‑tallest peak, Squaw Peak, was renamed Piestewa Peak to honor Army Specialist Lori Ann Piestewa, the first Native American woman killed in combat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Phoenix%2C_Arizona",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "America West Arena, now the Desert Diamond Arena, opened in downtown Phoenix in 1992 before the Suns moved there in December 2003.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
